<title>BRAZIL: Brazil sells 3.975 bln reais in Treasury papers.</title>
<headline>Brazil sells 3.975 bln reais in Treasury papers.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank, on behalf of National Treasury, raised 3.975 billion reais during an auction Friday of Treasury letters, dealers said.</p>
<p>The series of 182-day National Treasury Letters, known as LTNs, is due in June 15 1997, and was sold at an overnight call money rate of 2.508 percent a month.</p>
<p>The result of the auction was in line with market expectations, dealers added.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418</p>
